.TH EMERALD 1 "2026-09-07" "emerald" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
emerald \- package and ports manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B emerald
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B emerald
manages ports, package installation, upgrades, removal, dependency inspection, repositories, and system updates. It uses the configured ports repositories and package database and must be run as root for operations that change the system.
.PP
The command name is followed by a subcommand. Use \fBemerald help\fR for the complete built-in list.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B build PORT
Build a package from a port.
.TP
.B cache [clean|list]
Inspect or clean cached sources and packages.
.TP
.B cat PORT
Print the port's build script (normally \fB@BUILD_SCRIPT@\fR).
.TP
.B config
Print the effective configuration and configured aliases/masks.
.TP
.B dependent PORT
List packages depending on PORT.
.TP
.B depends PORT
List direct dependencies of PORT.
.TP
.B deplist PORT...
Print dependency lists.
.TP
.B dup
Report duplicate installed packages.
.TP
.B files PORT
List files belonging to installed port.
.TP
.B foreign
List installed packages not provided by configured ports.
.TP
.B help
Show built-in help.
.TP
.B hook {pre|post} {install|upgrade|remove} PORT
Run a hook manually from PORT's unified install file. The command requires root privileges.
.TP
.B info PORT...
Show port/package metadata; package names may also be added to the world list as implemented by the command.
.TP
.B install PORT...
Build and install ports.
.TP
.B installed
List installed packages.
.TP
.B integrity
Check installed package integrity.
.TP
.B list
List available ports.
.TP
.B locate PATTERN
Locate files in package file lists.
.TP
.B missing-deps
Report missing dependencies.
.TP
.B orphan
List orphaned packages.
.TP
.B outdated
List installed packages with newer port versions.
.TP
.B path PORT
Print a port directory path.
.TP
.B provide FILE
Find packages providing FILE.
.TP
.B purge
Remove packages no longer needed.
.TP
.B redeps PORT...
Reinstall or rebuild dependencies as required.
.TP
.B remove PORT...
Remove packages.
.TP
.B search PATTERN
Search ports and package metadata.
.TP
.B sync
Synchronize configured repositories.
.TP
.B sysup
Upgrade the system while respecting masks.
.TP
.B trigger
Run package-manager post-install triggers.
.TP
.B upgrade PORT...
Upgrade packages.
.TP
.B world [add|remove|list] PORT...
Manage the explicitly requested package set.
.TP
.B alias {list|add REAL ALIAS|remove REAL}
Manage package aliases. Adding and removing aliases requires root.
.TP
.B mask {list|add PORT...|remove PORT...}
Manage ports excluded from \fBsysup\fR. Adding and removing masks requires root.
.TP
.B version
Print the Emerald version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.TP
.B -v, --verbose
Print additional information where supported.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Answer yes to confirmations where supported.
.TP
.B -k, --keep-going
Continue after a build or operation failure where supported.
.TP
.B --append-repo=PATH
Append a local repository to the search path. May be repeated.
.TP
.B --prepend-repo=PATH
Prepend a local repository to the search path. May be repeated.
.TP
.B --override-repo=PATH
Use a local repository instead of the corresponding configured repository. May be repeated.
.TP
.B --repo=PATH
Add a repository path for this invocation. May be repeated.
.TP
.B --repo-file=FILE
Use FILE instead of the configured repository file.
.TP
.B --config-file=FILE
Use FILE instead of the configured configuration file.
.TP
.B --alias-file=FILE
Use FILE instead of the configured alias file.
.TP
.B --mask-file=FILE
Use FILE instead of the configured mask file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/emerald.conf
Build and runtime configuration.
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/emerald.repo
Repository definitions.
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/emerald.alias
Package aliases.
.TP
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/emerald.mask
Ports excluded from system upgrades.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. A non-zero status indicates invalid input, an unavailable port/package, a failed operation, or (for checks such as missing dependencies) a detected problem.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgadd (1),
.BR pkgbuild (1),
.BR pkgdel (1),
.BR portsync (1),
.BR revdep (1),
.BR emerald.conf (5)
